From b5196523cc1e822cf27350234013e697cdd52ffd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 06:11:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] perf(render): cache door platform scans per chunk epoch

canOpenDoors rescanned every cell around each open doorway of every stopped
vehicle and lift each frame, allocating block position, state and block
wrappers per cell. Cache the scan result keyed by the exact cells visited by
the original double loops. Entries stay valid only while every chunk column
read is the same chunk object with the same door-scan epoch; a client-only
WorldChunk mixin bumps the epoch when a platform or platform door block is
placed, removed or changed, or the chunk is reloaded from a packet. Door
values are still applied to freshly looked-up block entities on every call,
and oversized ranges or untracked chunks keep the original scan.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TD7PJ5R7t7hM3ymeeqXP4H
